#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# conservation_law_multipliers

#% text
# `conservation_law_multipliers(eq, u, x)` gives a basis of the multipliers of the differential equation `eq` for `u` of `x`: functions `Lambda` of the independent variables and of `u` with `Lambda eq` a total divergence for every function `u`, that is, `E_u(Lambda eq) == 0` for the Euler operator `E_u`. Each multiplier gives a conservation law (`conservation_laws`).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `order: q` lets the multipliers depend on the derivatives of `u` up to order `q` (for several independent variables, the derivatives in the first one, as for an evolution equation `u_t == F`). The default is 0.

#% item
# The condition `E_u(Lambda eq) == 0` is split by the powers of the derivatives `Lambda` does not depend on and solved like the determining equations of `lie_point_symmetries`. An infinite family is given as `conditional_expression(c(1)(...), cond)`. `degree: d` looks for multipliers that are polynomials of total degree at most `d` instead (useful for ordinary differential equations, whose multipliers of order 1 form an infinite family).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# The Korteweg-de Vries equation: mass, momentum and the Galilean law:

#% cell
conservation_law_multipliers(derivative(0, 1)(u)(x, t) + u(x, t)*derivative(1, 0)(u)(x, t) + derivative(3, 0)(u)(x, t) == 0, u, [x, t])
#% output
#= [u(x, t), -x + t*u(x, t), 1]

#% text
# With multipliers of order 2 the energy appears:

#% cell
conservation_law_multipliers(derivative(0, 1)(u)(x, t) + u(x, t)*derivative(1, 0)(u)(x, t) + derivative(3, 0)(u)(x, t) == 0, u, [x, t], order: 2)
#% output
#= [(1/2)*u(x, t)^2 + derivative(2, 0)(u)(x, t), u(x, t), -x + t*u(x, t), 1]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The multipliers of the heat equation are the solutions of the backward heat equation:

#% cell
conservation_law_multipliers(derivative(0, 1)(u)(x, t) == derivative(2, 0)(u)(x, t), u, [x, t])
#% output
#= [conditional_expression(c(1)(x, t), -derivative(0, 1)(c(1))(x, t) - derivative(2, 0)(c(1))(x, t) == 0)]

#% text
# Integrating factors of an ordinary differential equation:

#% cell
conservation_law_multipliers(y''(x) + y(x) == 0, y, x)
#% output
#= [cos(x), sin(x)]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `conservation_laws`, `lie_point_symmetries`
